coming from Turtle Rock Studios the same  studio behind the original left of dead  if bolt takes the four player co-op  experience and turns it on its head with  four versus one gameplay instead of  fighting off hundreds of zombies all  taking on an alien horde here there's  just one player controlled opponent for  you to tackle a giant flesh-eating and  thoroughly mean-looking monster well it  may look like there's little more to the  monster than an impressively sharp set  of teeth and some muscles you can just  as easily play a strategic stealth game  as you can an aggressive one than either  way it's a hell of a lot fun evolve will  feature different types of monster but  this charming chap here is called  Goliath as his name suggests Goliath is  no shrinking violet his physical  attributes are impressive letting him  rip boulders from the ground to hurl at  hunters at range and unleashes stream  the firing depth in his mouth she's too  evolved Goliath by eating animals and  you can make him bigger and stronger  with access to more abilities it's a  strategic decision to make though and  not only do you leave yourself  vulnerable to attack while evolving for  the discarded animal corpses and  footprints you leave make you easy prey  for a hunter there are four classes of  hunter in evolved assault trapper medic  and support each with their own set of  skills and a clearly defined role to  play within the team and you really do  need to play as a team in order to take  down the monster the balance between the  four hunter classes is impressive trying  to go it alone as any of them won't get  you very far  the assault class needs to be buffed and  healed to Landy's attacks the support  and medic classes need the offensive  firepower of assault to keep themselves  protected and they all need the skills  of the trapper to help them find and  incapacitate the monster voice chat  seems all but essential to get the most  out of the game if that balance was off  even by just a little bit then evolve  wouldn't have been nearly as fun to play  as it was this is a source of game that  people are going to tell stories about  after they're done playing four versus  one is a simple idea but the level of  depth that Turtle Rock is extracted from  the idea even in this early demo  surprised me and with more types of  monster on the way I can only see it  getting deeper a shooter it may be but  evolve is one of the most unique ideas  I've seen in a while and a well-executed  one at man definitely one to watch
 

